# Lines tools/qemu-test must see, in this order, as whole serial lines.
# QEMU's fw_cfg device writes into the PD's DMA region by the
# physical address the PD learned, and a transfer past the end of the region
# is refused before the device sees it.
NOWAYOS: dma-demo: starting
NOWAYOS: dma-demo: found QEMU's fw_cfg device, with DMA
NOWAYOS: dma-demo: the device wrote "QEMU" into the DMA region by its physical address
NOWAYOS: dma-demo: a transfer past the end of the region was refused before the device saw it
NOWAYOS: dma-demo: done

# Output that fails the test at once if it appears anywhere (substring match):
# a fault reported by the Microkit monitor, a kernel error message, a panic,
# or the PD giving up.
!MON|ERROR
!seL4(CPU
!panicked
!gave up
